# gh board guard rules for Codex CLI (execpolicy), the second layer under
# the PreToolUse hook because a hook failure does not block in Codex.
# Generated by gh board agent install --agent codex from the kit's embedded
# patterns: one prefix_rule per spelling whose only star is the trailing one,
# in patterns.json order; the shells Codex runs commands with are never
# forbidden here, the hook covers them. Do not edit; run the installer
# again to update.
# Prefix rules cannot express methods after a path, arbitrary option order,
# GraphQL bodies, absolute paths, shell scripts, or case-insensitive programs.
# Generated spellings include gh.exe and all method case combinations when
# the method precedes the path. Other program casing and shell forms require
# the kit's guard check hook. Subcommands remain case sensitive.
# Strict mode: off
prefix_rule(pattern=["gh", "project", "close"], decision="forbidden", justification="gh board guard denies gh project close")
prefix_rule(pattern=["gh.exe", "project", "close"], decision="forbidden", justification="gh board guard denies gh.exe project close")
prefix_rule(pattern=["gh", "project", "copy"], decision="forbidden", justification="gh board guard denies gh project copy")
